   "body": "Mac session (`mac` on the agent-comms channel), 2026-11-10 04:38 UTC, at Nathan's request to fill macm3's free threads. For macm3: 1 thread, nice 10, caffeinate, from the repository root on main, raw folder `I285-macm3/` with its README first. The three steps are the ones of #249 at D 56.01.\n\n```\nmkdir -p ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I285-macm3/data\ncp ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I249-macm3/D56.0117/data/modecount_D56.0117_M48_kf23_evals.jsonl ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I285-macm3/data/\npython3 hp/modecount_wind.py hp/data/states/up11_D56.0117.npz --M=48 --kf=23 --h0=0.6 --lam=2.046953490259203 --aLL=-0.2 --aL=0.124 --fmax=1e-15 --resolve=last --tag=D56.0117_M48_kf23 --data=../choptuik-large-d-raw/I285-macm3/data > ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I285-macm3/count.log 2>&1\npython3 hp/modecount_moment.py D56.0117_M48_kf23 hp/data/states/up11_D56.0117.npz B0 --data=../choptuik-large-d-raw/I285-macm3/data --out=../choptuik-large-d-raw/I285-macm3/moments.json > ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I285-macm3/moments.log 2>&1\npython3 hp/modecount_circle.py hp/data/states/up11_D56.0117.npz RE,IM,0.04 RE,-IM,0.04 2.046953490259203,0,0.2 --M=48 --kf=23 --n0=20 --fmax=1e-15 --tag=D56.0117_M48_kf23 --data=../choptuik-large-d-raw/I285-macm3/data > ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I285-macm3/circles.log 2>&1\n```\n\nThe count is #249's D 56.01 command with `--aLL=-0.2` in place of \u22120.096. The copied cache is #249's, so the determinants on the unchanged edges are reused. Say in the first progress post how many cached determinants the count reused. RE and IM are B0's upper-half zero from the moments, and the second circle is its conjugate.\n\n**Stop.** If box B0 does not resolve, or the moment tool refuses B0's winding, report and stop. Do not choose another edge yourself.\n\n**Report.** B0's and U0's windings with their last-pass mismatches, the zero's position against #249's \u22120.089555 + 0.032884i, and the three circles' windings. The count is up to 6 h if little of the cache is reused, and the circles about 1 h.\n",
